  (global_label "GND" (shape passive) (at 314.96 93.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "82f051eb-aabe-5cf6-a672-99d547461bd5")
    (property "Intersheetrefs" "" (at 314.96 93.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide)))
  (text "Power: the switch common is the 3.3 V rail (XIAO 3V3 pin). Position 1 = badge 3.3 V feeds the rail. Position 2 (OFF) ties D1 to the rail through R1; position 3 (USB-BAT) leaves the badge disconnected." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "61db7b44-2802-5cd4-a142-96b0dd4fb19e"))
  (text "On USB-BAT the XIAO powers itself from USB-C or the LiPo on J2 (which it charges). Do not plug in USB with the switch on SAO while on a badge: two 3.3 V regulators would share one rail." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 163.83 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d8fa2240-f6a6-5cd3-97a0-347e840e4119"))
  (text "The maker's five bicolour LEDs (D1-D5 = his LED1-LED5) keep his wiring: every blue anode on one pin, every red anode on another, one resistor each. Blue: D3 through 330 ohm (about 1.5 mA each). Red: D10 through 1.3 k (about 1.1 mA each). His were 22 ohm on an ATtiny85." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 167.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e06f8a60-21d9-5aa4-b469-f30d86c1ebcd"))
  (text "R2, R3: 330 ohm on the SAO GPIO pins per docs/standard.md. R1: 330 ohm in the OFF sense line. No I2C pull-ups on the add-on (the maker had 10 k; the badge provides them)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 171.45 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "24ed9a20-89bf-5ade-b390-5d63ea7590f1"))
  (text "Dropped from the maker's circuit: ATtiny85, its 10 k reset pull-up, the two 10 k I2C pull-ups, two 0 ohm links and the six ISP pogo pads. Mode button = the XIAO's BOOT button." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 175.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "abe3e710-4ec5-5402-a58f-6ff639372b32"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
